    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38843" root="ملأَ" body-key="m">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَمْلُوْءٌ</span></b> , pass. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلَأَ</span>, <i>Filled.</i> (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
Also, (assumed tropical:)  <i>Having the disease called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَآءَة</span>: as part.
n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلِئَ</span>. (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also, (and accord. to some
copies of the K, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلْآن</span></b> ,) <i>Affected</i> by God <i>with
that disease:</i> extr. [with respect to rule], (S, K,)
as it is used in the sense of the pass. part. n. of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمْلَأَ</span>: by rule it should be <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُمْلَأٌ</span>. (TA.)

